From: qvac
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Wan 2.1 I2V: bypass spatial VAE tiling for video encode/decode

When vae_tiling is enabled, vae_encode() and decode_first_stage() use a 2D
spatial tiling path that is incompatible with the 4D video tensors produced
by the Wan video VAE.

ENCODE: vae_encode() pre-allocates its result as [W/8, H/8, z_dim, batch].
For Wan 2.1 I2V the WanVAE encoder produces [W/8, H/8, t_latent, z_dim].
Passing encode_video=false (the default) hits the tiling branch and produces
a transposed tensor [62, 78, 16, 3] instead of [62, 78, 9, 16].
process_latent_in() then asserts ne[3]==16 but finds 3, crashing:
  GGML_ASSERT(latent->ne[channel_dim] == 16 || ...) failed

DECODE: decode_first_stage() checks vae_tiling_params.enabled without a
!decode_video guard. The Wan video latent [W/8, H/8, t_latent, z_dim] is
fed through the 2D tiling path, which produces all-black (zero) output
frames because the temporal/channel dimensions are misinterpreted.

Fix: add encode_video=true to the Wan 2.1 I2V concat-latent encode call,
and add !decode_video guard to the tiling branch in decode_first_stage().

--- a/src/stable-diffusion.cpp
+++ b/src/stable-diffusion.cpp
@@ -4098,7 +4098,7 @@ SDCPP_API sd_video_t* generate_video(sd_ctx_t* sd_ctx,
         });
 
-        concat_latent = sd_ctx->sd->encode_first_stage(work_ctx, image);
+        concat_latent = sd_ctx->sd->encode_first_stage(work_ctx, image, true);  // encode_video=true bypasses spatial tiling
 
@@ -2805,7 +2805,7 @@ SDCPP_API sd_video_t* generate_video(sd_ctx_t* sd_ctx,
             process_latent_out(x);
-            if (vae_tiling_params.enabled) {
+            if (vae_tiling_params.enabled && !decode_video) {
